          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Be the first to 'Go Out' by melding all cards in your hand except for one final discard, while maximizing your score through high-value melds.",
          gameplay: '1. **Direction**: Play proceeds counter-clockwise. 2. **Turn**: Each turn consists of drawing one card (from Stock or Ground) and discarding one card. 3. **Melding**: A player may place valid melds face up on the table once they meet the minimum requirements (often a single 50-point meld or a specific sequence length).',
          keyRules: [
            'Wild cards can be reused: If a player holds the natural card that a wild card represents on the table, they can swap it and take the wild card into their hand.',
            'Aces can be High (Q-K-A) or Low (A-2-3) but not both (K-A-2 is illegal).',
            'The discard pile (Ground) can only be picked up if the top card is immediately used in a meld.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Keep your Banakil (Wilds) hidden in your hand until you are ready to meld multiple sequences at once. This prevents opponents from seeing your progress.',
          intermediate: "If an opponent picks up from 'the Ground', they are close to finishing. Try to discard cards of suits they likely don't need based on their previous discards.",
          advanced: "The Swap: Look for an opponent's wild card on the table that you can replace with a natural card. Getting a wild card into your hand without drawing it is the most efficient way to 'Go Out'.",
          tips: [
            "Don't hoard 20-point wilds for too long; if someone goes out early, those wilds become massive negative points in your hand.",
            "Check the ground frequently. If many 10s have been discarded, don't try to build a set of 10s.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
